    *Study Design:*: Top-journal clinical review; synthesizes pyridostigmine evidence.
    *Certainty / population / discounted:*: raw 0.70 | POTS 0.80 | discounted 0.56
    *Key Findings:*:
        - Pyridostigmine is a low-level evidence-supported POTS treatment; dosing is limited by muscarinic side effects (GI cramping, salivation, urinary urgency).
        - Start-low-titrate approach is standard to find the individual cholinergic threshold.
    *Conclusion:*: The pyridostigmine therapeutic window is narrow and dose-limited by cholinergic side effects.
    *Limitations:*: Review; POTS population (not ME/CFS).

